  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering CSOs to Combat Human Trafficking in Sri Lanka (SL)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Sri Lanka):  Through the Empowering Civil Society Organizations to Combat Human Trafficking in Sri Lanka (ECCT) activity, USAID strengthens civil society at national and district levels to protect the rights of migrants.USAID will use FY2022 resources to strengthen policies and mechanisms to address human trafficking related crimes, identify, protect and refer victims of trafficking and communities at risk, and to encourage safe migration practices among those seeking to migrate. USAID will closely work with government stakeholders at both the national and local level and foster close collaborative links spanning across five provinces in Sri Lanka.Through ECCT activity, USAID will also work with selected civil society organizations (CSO) from the North Central Province of Sri Lanka to train them on issues related to human trafficking so that they may create awareness among their communities and contribute to policy advocacy. The CSOs will be introduced to journalists from the locality so that they may feed into each other&apos;s work on human trafficking and work in collaboration to address this issue. Local media will also be invited to provide coverage to trafficking that takes place at the grassroots level.USAID will also train youth on human trafficking to create champions and foster awareness of risk among youth networks. Most youth remain unaware of the dangers of human trafficking despite the surge in foreign employment migration in the country.Through this activity, USAID advances the Integrated Country Strategy Mission Objective 2.3: &apos;Bolster civil society and free and independent media in their efforts to promote democratic governance and respect for human rights among the Sri Lankan public&apos;. This activity also supports the USAID Country Development Cooperation Strategy Development Objective 1: &apos;Effective, Democratic Governance Strengthened&apos;.$300,000 within this IM contributes to the TIP earmark of $350,000.. .</narrative>
  </description>
